--->how can we rename the files......?
there are two ways ..........
1)We can perform that through UI
2)Using mv (move command) command
what is the difference that made by renaming the file name through ui directly or by using the command......?
The difference is that if we perform the renaming of file manually then it shows that the file was untracked because the file was not updated using git commands
Git assumes that we have deleted that file as that file was not present with the previous name like (demo.html --> demo1.html) and it assumes that the renamed one wsa the new file
So these is where git was got confused, to make sure that gir was not confused we have to work with the git command only to rename the file name
git mv old_filename new_filename (git mv demo.html demo1.html) - to rename file using git command
Then after performing these command we can observe a change that if we do that process manually we see U(Untracked) at the file name.
But now by using the command we can see the R(Renamed) at the end of the file name in green color
After passing these wew can perform git commit command to save our changes(dont forget to do that if we skip these our changes are not yet saved)

