---->If we modify anything in our file and added and commited it then if we perform the git checkout operation on that ............?
As a result the modified part was not removed as it was added and commited there
so to resolve these issue as we want to go back to the previous change .............?
1)git log - to know the commited information
2)git reset --soft HEAD-1 - It undo the commit but keeps the changes staged(adding area it is going to be right but it is going to undo the commit)
   it undo the commit section but it is still keeping it into the add zone
3)git commit -m "reset soft command"  - it saves all our changes
4)git reset --hard HEAD-1  - It undo the commit section and not keeps the changes staged which mean there wer not present in the adding area also


