---->stashing :

1)git stash                  -  These command remove the modified version of the file but it is going to keep it safe into the git stash list
2)git stash list             -  We can visit the git stash list through the command
3)git stash drop             -  we can delete the stash
4)git stash list             -  We can now check the git stash list status through the command
5)git stash drop stash@{0}   -  we can delete the specific stash through the stash id
6)git stash clear            -  we can delete all the stashes all together
7)                           -  we can apply last stash then without deleting it then we can simply write

1)we have modified one line in one of our files and before adding or commiting or pushing it we perform (git stash)
now when ever we go through the git stash command the modified line in that file was not appear at now
2)As a result of git stash list command, we can see the stash@{0} - think of it like an array with 0 as a stash number
3)these git stash drop was only for the latest stash, then what if we have multiple stashes...........?
Then what we can do means......
git stash drop stash_id (git stash drop stash@{0})
