----->git tag :
It was a mark.
If we want to remember one commit specifically then we can include a bookmark to that commit which was called as git tag.
Here git tag was used to mark a specific point(checkpoint,bookmark)

Example :
we know that some commits are very important for us where it plays a important role in our entire website
Now without keeping any mark I repeatedly performed hundreds of commits and now i want to remember that specific important commit
It was very hard for me to remember, so what if i have a bookmark(immediately we are able to find it or indexing it) it  right, so for that we are using tags

*)In repository commit history whenever we want to see some typical/major events into git history,then we can do that with the help of using git tags

There are two types of tags ...........
1)lightweight
2)Annotated weight(Giving extra information with git tag)

Usage of these tags........
1)firstly modify a file with some important message within that
2)add and commit that file
3)git tag v1.0        - For the specified modified message which was added and commited lastly was given with a tag v1.0
4)git log --oneline   - these command gives the #ids and the message rather than the entire information
5)git tag             - It helps when we want to get information of the tag later on as it give tag name like v1.0 like that
6)git show v1.0       - Shows the information at point that we performed this tag(simply it can say about when we used this tag)
7)                    - Using these we can include message along with the tag

